    {
      "id": "steady",
      "label": "Steady growth",
      "reason": "Prices rise by 2.0% and earnings by 3.7% every year. These are the long-run averages the Office for Budget Responsibility assumes in its July 2026 report. Earnings are always the highest measure, so the triple lock, the double lock and the earnings link give the same result. The rule announced for April 2030 follows earnings too, but can differ from the earnings link by up to 10p a week, because its earnings target is rounded once rather than each year.",
