      "id": "volatile",
      "label": "Volatile prices",
      "reason": "Years of high inflation and low pay growth (6.0% and 2.0%) alternate with years of low inflation and catch-up pay growth (1.0% and 5.0%). It shows how rules that take the higher measure each year pull ahead of both prices and earnings. The rule announced for April 2030 takes prices or 2.5% each year and stays above its earnings target, so it never needs to catch up.",
