      "label": "A year of falling earnings",
      "menu_label": "Falling earnings",
      "reason": "Earnings fall by 1.0% in the first year while prices rise by 1.0%. Pay then recovers by 6.0% with prices up 3.0%, and later years are steady at 2.0% and 3.5%. It tests negative growth and the cash floor. With the cash floor on, the rule announced for April 2030 ends lower than the earnings link: its earnings target counts the fall in pay, while the cash floor holds the earnings link still in that year.",
